IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-amount-helpers`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division B -- sections 15, 15.1, 15.2 and 15.3: THE SALARY AND WAGES ON WHICH A
-- CONTRIBUTION HAS BEEN MADE.
--
-- Section 15 works back from the amounts deducted from an employee's remuneration to the salary and wages on which a base
-- contribution (15), a first additional contribution (15.1) and a second additional contribution (15.2) has been made. Those
-- figures are what the self-employed contribution (section 10) and the election of subsection 13(3) subtract.
--
-- The formulas are encoded as the text words them. Read literally, paragraph (b) of subsection 15(1) is the aggregate
-- deducted, minus (the amount of 8(2)(b) plus (the same aggregate minus the amounts of 8(2)(a) and (b))), which is the amount
-- of 8(2)(a); so the greater of (a) and (b) is the amount of 8(2)(a) whenever (a) is not larger (NOTES.md, finding).
--
-- The "aggregates" take in what subsections (1.1) and (2) add: the caller adds the result of `s 15(1.1)` (an employer's failure to
-- deduct, notified in time) and `s 15(2)` (an amount the employer pays) to the amounts actually deducted.
--
-- out of range: section 21 (piece cp2): the amounts the employer deducts, and the return the employer files under subsection 15.3.
-- out of range: Schedule 1 and Schedule 2 (piece cp6): the rates.
-- The "prescribed circumstances" of section 15.3 are not stated in the Regulations file (a search of it for "15.3" finds nothing): a plain input.
-- out of range: regulations 22(4) and 34.1(2) (piece cr1) say that paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act does not apply to some employment included in pensionable employment by regulation; this module does not model that disapplication (it is in the Regulations' piece).
-- The amounts "determined under" subsection 8(2) are the rules of cp1-div-a-employee-employer-contributions.l4; the caller passes them.

§ `Division B -- Calculation of Contributions`

§§ `Section 15 -- the salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made`

-- src:444 | Amount of salary and wages on which base contribution made
-- src:445 | 15 (1) The amount of a person’s salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year is the greater of the following amounts, divided by the contribution rate for employees for the year:
-- src:446 | (a) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee’s base contribution for the year under this Act, minus the portion of those amounts that exceeds the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a), and
-- src:447 | (b) an amount equal to
-- src:448 | (i) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee’s base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan,
-- src:449 | minus
-- src:450 | (ii) the sum of
-- src:451 | (A) the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b), and
-- src:452 | (B) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee’s base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a) and (b).
@ref Act s 15(1) (src:445-452)
GIVEN `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year`
        `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
        `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act`
        `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`
        `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)`
        `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)`
    MEANS
        -- "the greater of the following amounts, divided by the contribution rate for employees for the year"; a rate of nil leaves nothing to divide by
        IF `the contribution rate for employees for the year` EQUALS 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST ((max `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`) DIVIDED BY `the contribution rate for employees for the year`)
    WHERE
        -- (a) the aggregate deducted under this Act, minus the portion of those amounts that exceeds the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act`
            MINUS (`the amount by which one amount exceeds another`
                       `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act`
                       `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)`)
        -- (b) (i) the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial plan, minus (ii) the sum of (A) the amount determined under 8(2)(b) and (B)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`
            MINUS (`the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)` PLUS `clause (B)`)
        -- (B) the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a) and (b)
        `clause (B)` MEANS
            `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`
            MINUS (`the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)` PLUS `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)`)

-- Clause 15(1)(b)(ii)(B), which subsection 15.2(1) refers to by number.
@ref Act s 15(1)(b)(ii)(B) (src:452)
GIVEN `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 15(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a) and (b)` `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)` `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)` MEANS
    `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's base contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`
    MINUS (`the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)` PLUS `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)`)

-- Not a provision: subsections 15(1.1), 15.1(1.1) and 15.2(1.1) say the same thing for the three tiers. If an employer has
-- failed to deduct an amount as required, and the person has, before June 30 of the following year, notified the Minister of the
-- failure, the amount that should have been deducted is added to the aggregate deducted. "Before June 30": a notice on June 30 is late.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the person's remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount that should have been deducted by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `date the person notified the Minister of the employer's failure to deduct that amount` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount added to the aggregate deducted for an employer's failure to deduct` year `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the person's remuneration` `the amount that should have been deducted by the employer` `date the person notified the Minister of the employer's failure to deduct that amount` MEANS
    IF `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the person's remuneration`
    THEN (CONSIDER `date the person notified the Minister of the employer's failure to deduct that amount`
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
          WHEN JUST notified THEN
              IF notified LESS THAN YMD (year PLUS 1) 6 30
              THEN JUST `the amount that should have been deducted by the employer`
              ELSE NOTHING)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:453 | Employer’s failure to deduct amount
-- src:454 | (1.1) For the purposes of subsection (1), if an employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the person’s remuneration on account of the employee’s base contribution for the year and that person has, before June 30 of the following year, notified the Minister of the employer’s failure to so deduct that amount, an amount equal to the amount that should have been so deducted by the employer on account of that contribution is added to the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee’s base contribution for the year.
@ref Act s 15(1.1) (src:453-454)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the person's remuneration on account of the employee's base contribution for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount that should have been deducted by the employer on account of that contribution` IS A NUMBER
      `date the person notified the Minister of the employer's failure to deduct that amount` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` year `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the person's remuneration on account of the employee's base contribution for the year` `the amount that should have been deducted by the employer on account of that contribution` `date the person notified the Minister of the employer's failure to deduct that amount` MEANS
    `the amount added to the aggregate deducted for an employer's failure to deduct`
        year
        `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the person's remuneration on account of the employee's base contribution for the year`
        `the amount that should have been deducted by the employer on account of that contribution`
        `date the person notified the Minister of the employer's failure to deduct that amount`

-- Not a provision: subsections 15(2), 15.1(2) and 15.2(2) say the same thing for the three tiers. An amount the employer failed to
-- deduct and then pays on account of the contribution is deemed to have been deducted.
GIVEN `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the employee's remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the employer pays on account of the contribution for that year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount deemed to have been deducted when the employer pays an amount it failed to deduct` `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the employee's remuneration` `the amount the employer pays on account of the contribution for that year` MEANS
    IF `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the employee's remuneration`
    THEN JUST `the amount the employer pays on account of the contribution for that year`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:455 | Effect of payment by employer of amount not deducted as required
-- src:456 | (2) For the purposes of subsection 8(2) and this section, if an amount that an employer has failed to deduct as required from the remuneration of an employee on account of the employee’s base contribution for a year is paid by the employer on account of the employee’s base contribution for that year, the amount so paid is deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of that contribution.
@ref Act s 15(2) (src:455-456)
GIVEN `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the remuneration of an employee on account of the employee's base contribution for a year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount paid by the employer on account of the employee's base contribution for that year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 15(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the base contribution` `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the remuneration of an employee on account of the employee's base contribution for a year` `the amount paid by the employer on account of the employee's base contribution for that year` MEANS
    `the amount deemed to have been deducted when the employer pays an amount it failed to deduct`
        `the employer has failed to deduct an amount as required from the remuneration of an employee on account of the employee's base contribution for a year`
        `the amount paid by the employer on account of the employee's base contribution for that year`

§§ `Section 15.1 -- the salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made`

-- src:457 | Amount of salary and wages on which first additional contribution made
-- src:458 | 15.1 (1) The amount of a person’s salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for a year is the greater of the following amounts, divided by the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year:
-- src:459 | (a) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee’s first additional contribution for the year under this Act, minus the portion of those amounts that exceeds the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1), and
-- src:460 | (b) an amount equal to
-- src:461 | (i) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee’s first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan,
-- src:462 | minus
-- src:463 | (ii) the sum of
-- src:464 | (A) the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c), and
-- src:465 | (B) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee’s first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a.1) and (c).
@ref Act s 15.1(1) (src:458-465)
GIVEN `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 15.1(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for a year`
        `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
        `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act`
        `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`
        `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)`
        `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)`
    MEANS
        IF `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` EQUALS 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST ((max `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`) DIVIDED BY `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act`
            MINUS (`the amount by which one amount exceeds another`
                       `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act`
                       `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)`)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`
            MINUS (`the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)` PLUS `clause (B)`)
        `clause (B)` MEANS
            `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`
            MINUS (`the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)` PLUS `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)`)

@ref Act s 15.1(1)(b)(ii)(B) (src:465)
GIVEN `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 15.1(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a.1) and (c)` `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)` `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)` MEANS
    `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that person on account of the employee's first additional contribution for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`
    MINUS (`the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)` PLUS `the amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)`)

